// A2 course (A1 → A2 roadmap), module 17 „Plaanid, kokkulepped ja tulevik” (a2-081…085), level A2, in the final shape
// (docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_A2.md, row m17 = m1: LUGU KUUL AVAS PROB, with the leads of modules 11–19; gates V1–V16 of
// docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_B1.md §8). One storyline, October, a year before the B1 course (docs/COURSE_CAST.md). Sofia works at Tuul Logistika (boss Liis Laan,
// colleagues Anna and Markus, client Lepik); the autumn course at Keelekool Sõna meets on Mondays and Wednesdays at 18–20 (Maret, Aune, administrator Ene; Tom,
// Lucía, Dmitri, Olga, Sergei). Sunday 3 October: Sofia plans her week, and her mother Helgi rings: she comes on Friday 8 October and „not alone” (she brings
// neighbour Tiiu's cat Miisu). Saturday 9 October at 17 (first 16): dinner at Jaan's; Viktor fetches Helgi from the station on Friday at 18. The module product: the course's autumn trip to Haapsalu on Saturday 16 October
// (15 €, bus from the school at 9); on Thursday 14 October the bus firm can only come at 11. Pictures of the Kasuta sheets (art/visuals/a2-module-17.js):
// 081 Sofia plans the next day, 085 Anna and Sofia at the big calendar.
//   081 LUGU R→W  the future with the present and a time word (homme lähen, järgmisel nädalal, kuu pärast, varsti), kavatsen + da; corner S1 (picture and
//                 questions, S06, in Kasuta because that sheet has the picture); main: a 60–80-word text about my next week (W05), edited; S05 = `081_p_cal`.
//   082 KUUL L→W  a meeting agreed step by step (Kas … sobib?, Kahjuks ei saa, Aga kas …?, Äkki …?, mulle sobib, kinnitus); corner L3 (Ene on the trip, short
//                 answers); main: a 40–70-word message confirming or changing the meeting (W08), planned first.
//   083 AVAS R→S  kui + olevik, siis …; try first → rule → try again; corner R5 (Maret's letter, 8 gaps); main: the pair agrees plan A and plan B for the trip (S03).
//   084 PROB L→S  the plan breaks: hear what changed, try, language, try again (Kahjuks … jääb ära, Mis ajaks?, Selge, siis …); corner L4 (who does what,
//                 matching); main: the phone call that agrees a new time and place (S10).
//   085 EKS       the module exam, every part timed (B.examPart): R1–R5, W1, W2a, L1–L4, S0, S1, S2.
// Every teaching lesson: „Mäletad?” naming the previous lesson and one of modules 13–15, an in-lesson pair task, a home recording in Kasuta, two fluency
// tasks, one exam corner. No tingiv kõneviis (A2): „Aga kas … sobib?”, „Äkki …?”, never „Kuidas oleks …?”, „Kas sa saaksid …?”.
